   "evidence": "Line 14 \"at large hadron transverse momentum\" vs. lines 456-468 (`doubleConvStructureFunction_diagonal_ofDeltaDelta` = `\u2211 i, c i * f i x Q2 * D h i z Q2`) and lines 20-22 (\"at leading order it is `e_i\u00b2 \u03b4_{ij} \u03b4(1 - y) \u03b4(1 - w)`\"); the cited sources (Altarelli-Ellis-Martinelli-Pi 1979; de Florian-Stratmann-Vogelsang 1998) are for the transverse-momentum-integrated double convolution. The phrase matches the roadmap section title `### 1.1 The factorisation formula at large hadron transverse momentum` (roadmap/EpsilonEridaniRoadmaps/Hadronization/README.md:479).",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Factorization/SIDIS/Coefficient.lean",
   "fix": "Drop the regime clause: open with what is formalized, e.g. \"In collinear factorization of semi-inclusive deep-inelastic scattering, a structure function in the two momentum fractions is a double convolution ...\". Leave the roadmap's \u00a71.1 framing in the PR description, where the `Roadmap:` line records it.",
   "issue": "The module docstring claims the material is collinear factorization of SIDIS \"at large hadron transverse momentum\", but no transverse-momentum variable occurs anywhere in the file (`doubleConvStructureFunction C f D h x z Q2` has only the two momentum fractions and the scale), and the file's own leading-order theorem `doubleConvStructureFunction_diagonal_ofDeltaDelta` gives `\u2211\u1d62 c_i f_i (x) D_i (z)` from `e_i\u00b2 \u03b4(1-y) \u03b4(1-w)` \u2014 the P_hT-integrated leading order. At P_hT of order Q the coefficient function starts at O(\u03b1_s) and has no \u03b4(1-y)\u03b4(1-w) term, so the stated regime and the stated leading order cannot both hold.",
   "line": 14
  }
